rticle-title><source><italic>Physiological Genomics</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>17</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>230</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14762175</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Log-normalised intensity versus time for 130 genes. Foreach gene, the line joins the average value at each time point.Vertical dashed lines indicate time points.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.001" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Smoothed curves obtained forthe gene <italic>Cyp4a10</italic> with &#x003bb; = 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, and 0.8.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.002" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>First derivatives of smoothed curves obtained for thegene <italic>Cyp4a10</italic> (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="F2">Figure 2</xref>). Horizontal dottedline locates zero.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.003" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Influence of the smoothing parameter&#x003bb; on the proportion of variance explainedby the first six PCs. From left to right,&#x003bb; equals (a) 0.8, (b) 0.6, (c) 0.4, and (d) 0.2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.004" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F5"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Influence of the smoothing parameter &#x003bb; on the two firsteigenvectors (first: full line, second: dashed line) of the PCA. From left to right, &#x003bb; equals (a) 0.8, (b) 0.6, (c) 0.4, and (d) 0.2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.005" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F6"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Dendrogram representing the result of the hierarchicalclustering performed on the value of the first derivative smoothedcurves using Euclidean distance and Ward criterion.The horizontal lines locate the cut level identifying 4 clusters(hc1, &#x02026; , hc4).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.006" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F7"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Representation of the smooth curves distributed in 4 clusters determinedafter hierarchical and <italic>k</italic>-means classification.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.007" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F8"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>Representation of variables (discretized time points, onthe left) and individuals (genes, on the right) on the first twoprincipal components. Genes are differentially displayed accordingto their cluster after <italic>k</italic>-means.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.008" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F9"><label>Figure 9</label><caption><p>Heatmap of smoothed gene expression profiles for thewhole dataset. Genes are ordered according to their clusterdetermined by the <italic>k</italic>-means algorithm. Horizontal blue linesseparate the 4 clusters. Values increase from green to red <italic>via</italic> black.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.009" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F10"><label>Figure 10</label><caption><p>Heatmap of smoothedgene expression profiles without SCD1 and km4-genes.Graphical features are the same as <xref ref-type="fig" rid="F9">Figure 9</xref>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-70561.010" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Changes between hierarchical clustering and <italic>k</italic>-means clusters.</p></caption><table><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Clusters</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hc1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hc2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hc3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">hc4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sum</td></tr><tr><td colspan="6" rowspan="1"><hr/></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">km1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">26</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">29</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">km2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">74</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">km3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">24</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">km4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td></tr><tr><td colspan="6" rowspan="1"><hr/></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sum</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">54</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">130</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>